<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  ProcessFlow with arrivals that follow the clock: a service desk over a day with a morning and an evening peak (PRO: ProcessFlow).

  Customers arrive at a rate that changes through the day (customers an hour; the clock is in hours; straight lines between the points; the day repeats):
      00:00 to 07:00   4        08:30   120 (the morning peak)        10:00 to 16:00   30        17:15   120 (the evening peak)        19:00 to 24:00   4
  Four agents serve one first-come-first-served line, each taking 2 minutes on average (Exponential, 30 an hour). The desk's capacity is 120 an hour, equal to the
  rate at the top of each peak, so a line builds around the peaks and clears within the hour after.
  The arrival input is read in operational time: each draw is the number of customers expected before the next arrival, so an Exponential of rate 1 makes the arrivals
  a Poisson stream whose rate is the profile, exactly. The profile's integral over one day is 635.75 customers.
  One row is one customer who has left (output="entities"). Output columns, 6 per row: 0 the clock time (hours) the customer left, 1 customer number (in order of
  arrival), 2 hours in the desk, 3 hours waiting in the line, 4 hours in service, 5 visits (always 1).

  To run it:        grind with a count of 2000 on samples/pro/process-flow-day.xml        (about three days)
  What to look for: customer numbers climb by about 636 a day; waits are 0 at night and in the quiet hours and rise around each peak. Measured on 108 days of this
                    seed (the first two dropped), the mean wait of customers leaving in each hour is 1.8 minutes from 08:00, 1.2 from 09:00, 2.2 from 17:00 and 0.7 from 18:00,
                    and about 0 in every other hour; the mean over all customers is 0.84 minutes. Add agents or scale the rate (rateScale) to see how the peaks respond.
-->
<dataset columns="exitTime, customer, sojourn, wait, service, visits" seed="20261014">
  <root node="Desk"/>
  <nodes>
    <Exponential name="Gap" lambda="1.0"/>
    <Exponential name="Service" lambda="30.0"/>
    <ProcessFlow name="Desk" stations="Agent:4" output="entities"
                 rate="0:4, 7:4, 8.5:120, 10:30, 16:30, 17.25:120, 19:4" rateMode="linear" ratePeriod="24">
      <input name="Gap" role="arrival"/>
      <input name="Service" role="service.Agent"/>
    </ProcessFlow>
  </nodes>
</dataset>
